//   
//   ● The ck.vim syntax file is already copied to /usr/share/vim/vim91/syntax/, but .ck filetype
//     detection is missing from vim's filetype.vim. The cleanest fix is to add it to your
//     user-level ~/.vim/ directory instead of system files — no sudo needed, survives vim updates.
//   
//     Here's what to do:
//   
//     mkdir -p ~/.vim/ftdetect
//     echo 'au BufNewFile,BufRead *.ck setf ck' > ~/.vim/ftdetect/ck.vim
//   
//     This uses vim's ftdetect/ autoload mechanism — any .vim file dropped there is sourced
//     automatically for filetype detection. It will pick up the syntax from
//     /usr/share/vim/vim91/syntax/ck.vim that's already there.
//   
//     Run those two commands (you can prefix with ! to run them here in the session), then open a
//     .ck file and check with :set ft? — it should say filetype=ck.
//   
//     The old method (editing /usr/share/vim/vim91/filetype.vim directly) broke because vim
//     updates overwrite that file. The ~/.vim/ftdetect/ approach is the standard user-owned way to
//      add filetype detection permanently.
//   
//   ✻ Brewed for 39s
//   
//   ❯ can i put ck.vim in a user-level directory ?                                                
//   
//   ● Yes — put it in ~/.vim/syntax/ck.vim. Vim checks that before the system directory.
//   
//     mkdir -p ~/.vim/syntax
//     cp /home/toup/chuck/dev/TOOLS/syntax/ck.vim ~/.vim/syntax/
//   
//     Combined with the ftdetect file from before, everything lives in ~/.vim/ and nothing depends
//      on system files:
//   
//     ~/.vim/
//       syntax/ck.vim       ← the syntax rules
//       ftdetect/ck.vim     ← triggers it for *.ck files
//   
//   ✻ Brewed for 5s
//   
//   ※ recap: Adding ChucK vim syntax highlighting permanently via user-level config. Next step: 
//     run the two mkdir/cp commands to set up ~/.vim/syntax/ck.vim and ~/.vim/ftdetect/ck.vim. 
//     (disable recaps in /config)
//   
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

CLAUDE WAY in user space:

mkdir -p ~/.vim/ftdetect
echo 'au BufNewFile,BufRead *.ck setf ck' > ~/.vim/ftdetect/ck.vim
mkdir -p ~/.vim/syntax
cp /home/toup/chuck/dev/TOOLS/syntax/ck.vim ~/.vim/syntax/

